  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Tracheal Transplantation shows early but tangible scholarly and practical reach: it has one OpenAlex citation, 49 recorded downloads, and a teaching-related video signal, alongside open access availability through repository records.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Pierre Delaere\u2019s <em>Tracheal Transplantation</em> addresses a difficult problem in regenerative medicine: how to repair and transplant one of the body\u2019s most technically challenging airway structures. The book\u2019s impact record is still modest, but it is already visible in several different ways. OpenAlex records one citation, indicating that the work has begun to enter the scholarly literature, while OAPEN metrics show 49 downloads, suggesting that readers are finding and using the book in practice.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citing landscape points to a focused form of uptake in tissue engineering and tracheal regeneration. The single citing article appeared in 2025 in <em>ACS Biomaterials Science &amp; Engineering</em> and is centered on tubular tissue-engineered scaffolds and cellular seeding for tracheal repair. That pattern suggests the book is being used as background or methodological context by researchers working on adjacent regenerative approaches, rather than as a broadly cited general reference.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">There are also signs of educational and instructional value. The record includes a YouTube video titled \u201cMovie 1. Experimental tracheal transplantation,\u201d associated with the author, which points to use of the book\u2019s subject matter in a demonstrative or teaching context. In addition, the title is indexed in WorldCat and available through open repository records, which may help explain its visibility beyond a single citation track.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Taken together, the evidence portrays a specialized medical monograph with early scholarly traction, some reader demand, and clear relevance to regenerative medicine communities. The record does not support broader claims of large-scale impact, but it does show that the book has entered a niche research conversation and is being used in ways consistent with both scientific reference and educational dissemination.</p>",
